.3/elasticity holds do not\nblock this chapter. H-213-OPC2 blocks formal_output_choice_teaching only; leave\nit open. Currentness is permission to act, not evidence of finished teaching.\n\n## Build order and ownership\n\n1. §2.1.1 Kostenstructuren: first internal exemplar, independent plan review,\n   source/asset/PDF build, independent paragraph/quality and rendered review.\n2. §2.1.2 Opbrengsten, winst en break-even: after §2.1.1 teaching is reviewed.\n3. §2.1.3 Marginale kosten en marginale opbrengsten: after §§2.1.1–2.1.2.\n4. §2.1.4 Gemengde opgaven: after all three reviewed theory paragraphs; no new\n   theory and no paragraaf.* output.\n5. Chapter consistency review, then student and separate answer assembly.\n\nExact Part A plans beneath this chapter folder (all pending independent review):\n\n- `2.1.1 Kostenstructuren/2.1.1-textbook-plan.md`\n- `2.1.2 Opbrengsten, winst en break-even/2.1.2-textbook-plan.md`\n- `2.1.3 Marginale kosten en marginale opbrengsten/2.1.3-textbook-plan.md`\n- `2.1.4 Gemengde opgaven/2.1.4-textbook-plan.md`\n\nEach paragraph has a distinct builder agent in claimed isolated paired\nworktrees. Root alone coordinates/integrates. First builder:\nreleased_pin_analysis at C:/wt/book2-211-production-20260905/; independent\nparagraph-plan/review agent correction_plan_review; non-author QC/quality-ref\nspecialist assigned before acceptance. Further assignments precede authoring.\nBuilders do not produce their own independent review or quality-ref.\n\n## Prerequisites, retrieval and interleaving\n\n| Paragraph | Incoming operation and classification | Planned treatment and downstream use |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2.1.1 | A04 substitution/elementary division: previously_taught_retrieval_required, underbouw arithmetic evidenced by registry; Book1 cost familiarity: preview_or_familiarity_only; formal classifications/functions/averages: new_formal_learning | Retrieve substitution and unit check only; fully teach cost behaviour, totals and averages. No generic graph retrieval because target has no graph construction. Closing task revisits substitution with explicit model bounds. Prepares 212–214 and the later232 supply-as-MC bridge, not that bridge itself. |\n| 2.1.2 | Reviewed211 totals/averages: previously_taught_retrieval_required; Book1 straight-line coordinates/scales: retrieval-required, with paragraph-level source evidence | Retrieve TK and a pair of coordinates; teach TO, GO, profit, linear break-even and vertical profit distance. Closing interleaving contrasts cost/average meanings with revenue/profit. |\n| 2.1.3 | Reviewed211–212 totals/functions/profit: previously_taught_retrieval_required; interval-normalized marginal ratios: new_formal_learning | Retrieve totals then teach differences divided by the actual ΔQ. Closing interleaving distinguishes GTK=TK/Q from MK=ΔTK/ΔQ. Prepares214 and232, not optimization. |\n| 2.1.4 | All three reviewed routes, individually rechecked; curricular placement alone never proves secure learner knowledge | Mixed source selection, cost/revenue/profit/break-even/average/marginal comparison. If actual work reveals a gap, route support to the originating paragraph; add no fourth theory lesson. |\n\nParagraph plans name exact earlier sources and printed retrieval questions.\nPreviously taught is not synonymous with learner-secure. Retrieval weakness\nrequires explicit support before the dependent task, with optional support time\nseparate from the independently paced core. Start contains a brief check of the\nnewly taught example plus distinct genuine retrieval, not a relabelled new topic.\n\n## Shared contexts and model boundaries\n\nDe Korenaar in211: one month, Q=500–1,000, unchanged production capacity;\nhuur/verzekering440 + connection/subscription60 gives TCK500 €/month;\ningredients/packaging0.70 + oven usage0.10 gives TVK=0.80Q €/month.\nAt Q500 totals are500/400/900; at Q1,000 they are500/800/1,300.\nGCK/GVK/GTK are1.00/0.80/1.80 then0.50/0.80/1.30 €/brood.\nNo claim that all electricity is variable or all cost components fixed forever.\n\n§212 deliberately reuses TK=500+0.80Q, adds fixed P=1.50 €/brood and\nTO=1.50Q €/month; GO=P only for Q>0. Break-even continuous714.2857…;\n715 is the first whole bread count without loss. Graph intercepts describe the\nstated algebraic functions; drawing them is not evidence that the211 capacity\nassumption was empirically verified down to zero. At Q1,000 profit is a vertical\ndistance of200 €/month, never a shaded area. No marginal/optimal-output rule.\n\n§213 switches to the frozen Linea/Curva sources. MK and MO are interval averages\nper extra product, displayed at right endpoints, never derivatives or the raw\nrow difference. At Linea's10-product intervals MK3/MO8; Curva's5-product\nintervals MK5/15/25 and MO30. Constant price explains constant MO.\nDo not infer profit-maximizing output from the final table row or MO=MK.\n\nBefore214, §213 explicitly connects interval marginals to the vertical profit\ndistance taught in212: Δwinst=ΔTO−ΔTK, hence Δwinst/ΔQ=MO−MK over the same\ninterval. A worked two-interval comparison and one faded practice comparison\nshow why equal MO can accompany unequal profit increases when MK changes.\nFor example, over two10-product intervals with ΔTO80 each and ΔTK30 then50,\nprofit grows50 then30 euros:5 then3 euros per extra product. Use this bounded\nidentity to explain observed interval growth, not to choose optimal output.\nIt is explanatory scaffolding for the existing213/214 target chain, not a new\nterminal goal or derivative. Budget it by replacing repetitive marginal drills\nin the actual <=55-minute213 plan, never by appending unbudgeted core work.\n\n§214 SmoothBox: TCK1,200 €/day, variable2 €/lunchbox, price5 €/lunchbox,\nnormal capacity700/day. Beyond700 use supplied total-cost table, not a linear\nextrapolation of normal costs. Positive vertical profit distance grows fastest\nover Q400–700; compare normal production with every spoed interval.\nThe supplied completed curves remain supplied; students mark, not reconstruct.\n\n## Shared notation, visuals and procedures\n\nUse TK/TCK/TVK, GTK/GCK/GVK, TO/GO, MK/MO consistently; Q is contextual quantity,\nnot interchangeable with euros. Decimal comma and appropriate precision in\nstudent text; state total €/period versus average/marginal €/product in tables,\naxes and answers. Q>0 for average formulas. Use productiecapaciteit and explicitly\nbounded assumptions; no new formal proportional/degressive/progressive taxonomy.\n\nColour conventions: TK/TCK #E67E22, TO #1A5276, GTK #8E44AD; direct labels,\nline styles/markers and text meaning remain usable without colour. No decorative\ngraphs. Text, tables and SVG/PNG share exact values and model bounds.\n\n| Paragraph | Required meaningful visual support / student action |\n|---|---|\n| 211 | Behaviour classification; total-to-average formula map; same fixed-cost amount divided over more products. Diagrams support explanation; no unasked student graph construction. |\n| 212 | Paired TK/TO lines with break-even and a vertical profit bracket; fully modelled example, faded support, independent construction then exact target. No profit-area shading. |\n| 213 | Aligned total/interval tables and Δtotal/ΔQ annotation, with changing interval lengths explicit. Tables, not unrequested calculus/curve construction. |\n| 214 | Supplied full base graph and source table; student marks BE and interval. Answer asset overlays only requested marks and explains all comparisons. |\n\nPin exact asset names/geometry in each paragraph plan before generation.\nUse paired paragraph-prefixed SVG/PNG; reproducible sources live in platform.\n\nUnified answer procedure: identify quantities/period → select relation → show\nsubstitution → compute and label units → interpret and bound conclusion.\nClassification begins with total cost response to Q within capacity/time.\nCost functions sum constant and per-unit components before substituting.\nAverages divide each relevant total by the same Q and explain the unit.\nBreak-even sets TO=TK, solves and checks both sides, then separately handles\nwhole units. Marginals select an interval, show both differences and divide by\nΔQ, place at the right endpoint and interpret that interval. Reuse these exact\nprocedures in worked examples, practice and answers; reduce help, not reasoning.\n\n## Paper route, timing and review floor\n\nTheory paragraphs print the seven exercise stages, including optional guided\nsupport in the paper itself. Worked example precedes compact non-heading recap,\nthen Start. No website, QR, device or Part B dependency. Every goal is assessed\nand every answer responds to the actual prompt, including reasoning and units.\nProvide optional support without a separate low track and a substantive bonus.\n\nEach theory plan and final walkthrough must show an actual core lesson equation\nat <=55 minutes including motivation, instruction, example, recap, retrieval,\npractice, target and transitions. Optional guided support and bonus have separate\nbudgets; closing retrieval is explicitly in-class or homework. Frozen target\nestimates211≈11,212≈12,213≈12 minutes are design inputs, not measured timings.\nMixed214 target≈20 minutes gets its own actual source-reading/solve walkthrough.\nClassroom timing and learner attainment remain observation-dependent flags.\n\nIndependent reviews: plan, economics/precision, didactics, Dutch language,\nteacher-learning quality, student experience, full-page render/figure integrity,\nand separately generated schema2 Part A quality-ref. No core defect carried as\na minor flag. Preserve unrelated companion blocks and files unchanged.\n\n## Outputs, assembly and acceptance\n\nRetain the four existing paragraph folder names. Theory: paragraaf/opgaven/\nantwoorden .md/.html/.pdf; consolidation: opgaven/antwoorden only, with assets,\nthin build_pdf.py, textbook plan/review/quality-ref/handoff for each.\n\nChapter stem `2.1 Kosten en opbrengsten` with ` – hoofdstuk` and ` – antwoorden`\nin .md/.html/.pdf. Student assembly embeds each complete theory paragraph once\n(its exercises are already included), then214opgaven once. Answer assembly uses\nfour answer sources only. Never duplicate separate opgaven alongside paragraaf.\n\nChapter `_assets` copies must hash-match paragraph sources. build_chapter.py\ndelegates reusable generation to platform; the front page lists all goals with\nat least12pt body/table type, overriding the old11pt layout rule. Simplify layout\ninstead of shrinking. All final pages are rendered and inspected at normal scale.\n\nRequire paragraph part-a student-web AND publisher-print validation, chapter\nvalidation, exact target/source/asset/answer checks, source/output parity,\nindependent chapter consistency review and rendered proof manifest/contact sheet/\npage images. Review evidence and immutable plan commit/hash will be recorded in\nplatform `reports/sprints/BOOK2-TEXTBOOK-PRODUCTION-1-chapter-21-plan-review.md`.\nNo artifact existence or inherited review substitutes for this fresh evidence.\n",
