its A04 explicitly; micro-teaching-units.json A04 describes substitution and endpoint checks as earlier arithmetic. Start 1 retrieves these; a short solution reminder supports gaps without implying mastery from completion |\n| Graph/table prerequisite decision | Target supplies a classification table: teach its response columns here. No independent graph construction or generic graph-readiness test is required; supporting theory diagrams are explained fully |\n| Explicit non-goals | Revenue, profit, break-even, marginal costs, MO=MK, formal proportional/degressive/progressive classification; no optimization, calculus, long-route OP-C2 or Part B lesson components |\n| Downstream prepares-for | §§2.1.2–2.1.4; later supply-as-MC bridge in §2.3.2. Here only cost foundations, not that bridge itself |\n| Retrieval | Substitution, division and final answer unit checking only; no generic Book 1 quiz |\n| Interleaving | Earlier substitution and arithmetic remain embedded in every cost calculation; closing review revisits those operations without new theory |\n| Operation emphasis | Balanced behavior-based selection/classification, function construction, two-quantity calculation, total/average interpretation, trend explanation and claim evaluation |\n| Misconception boundary | Regular-looking invoice does not define constant cost; TCK is not GCK; TVK is not GVK; constant GVK is conditional; GTK need not halve when Q doubles |\n| Model conditions/relevant range | One stated month, positive Q in each specified range, unchanged capacity; constant per-unit variable coefficient only where supplied. No extrapolation to Q=0, new capacity, another month or an arbitrary cost model |\n\n### Open holds and current-action effect\n\nCurrent action for this drafting stage: goal_design (operational plan only;\nthe four approved goals and target bytes are not being redesigned).\nAll rows below refer to the exact hold by id in the pinned meta file.\nFor released holds, evidence aliases name the full reference and historical\nsubject below; release is not re-attributed to this author.\n\n| Hold ID | Status | Scope match? | Current action | In blocks? | In permits? | Resolution action? | Effect | Release evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| H-OUTLINE-OWNER | released | yes, book 2 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E1 |\n| H-211-GATE0B1 | released | yes, 2.1.1 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E2, historical goals |\n| H-211-TARGET-INTEGRATION | released | yes, 2.1.1 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E2, historical target/integration |\n| H-229-211-CANDIDATE | released | yes, 2.1.1 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, exact current 2.1.1 record |\n| H-212-STALE-REF | released | no, 2.1.2 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.1.2 |\n| H-213-DELTAQ | released | no, 2.1.3 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.1.3 |\n| H-229-214-CANDIDATE | released | no, 2.1.4 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.1.4 |\n| H-229-221-CANDIDATE | released | no, 2.2.1 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.2.1 |\n| H-229-222-CANDIDATE | released | no, 2.2.2 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.2.2 |\n| H-229-223-CANDIDATE | released | no, 2.2.3 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.2.3 |\n| H-229-224-CANDIDATE | released | no, 2.2.4 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.2.4 |\n| H-231-V5 | released | no, 2.3.1 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.3.1 |\n| H-232-V5 | released | no, 2.3.2 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.3.2 |\n| H-233-V5-REF | released | no, 2.3.3 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.3.3 |\n| H-234-PLACEHOLDER | released | no, 2.3.4 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject 2.3.4 |\n| H-213-OPC2 | open | no, 2.1.3/long route | goal_design | no | yes | no | NOT_APPLICABLE | null |\n| H-221-PRIOR | open | no, 2.2.1 | goal_design | no | yes | no | NOT_APPLICABLE | null |\n| H-22-ELASTIC-CONTRAST | open | no, 2.2.1–2.2.2 | goal_design | no | yes | no | NOT_APPLICABLE | null |\n| H-229-EI-SUPERSESSION | released | no, 2.2.3 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E4 |\n| H-BOOK2-ROOT-PLAN | open | yes, book 2 | goal_design | no | no | no | NOT_APPLICABLE, unrelated action | null |\n| H-CHAPTER-23-PLAN | open | no, chapter 2.3 | goal_design | no | yes | no | NOT_APPLICABLE | null |\n| H-MERGE-GOVERNANCE | released | yes, book 2 | goal_design | no | no | no | RELEASED | E5, historical payload only |\n\nE1: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/pull/226#issuecomment-5515033629;\nmeijer1973, 2026-09-02, original outline\n69d803d2786e97bbd7519d2feed3ee29b79751b00a3c8a440432621927a13cde.\nE2: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/pull/227#issuecomment-5524345692;\nmeijer1973, 2026-09-03; historical goals\nafda7a196ae5ea9e1d23207158c33c1b32c5f5ebc928752c3fe4b54d5172a560,\nhistorical target 709535d15ab3c89b7cfe3bac27ae9a152044cbd7611057b3bdf0defec1cc3f34,\nhistorical integration 30e0d5c2f71c64ee31ecadb614559d9431d392a5.\nE3: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/blob/6e35f4fe0aeaa448da9476469294ccd45775232d/reports/sprints/BOOK2-TARGET-INTEGRATION-1-owner-authorization.md;\nmeijer1973, 2026-09-05, integrated_commit\n206c018478654db781cc879e7ea36adcd9ef600c for each of the twelve holds;\neach exact subject hash remains in that hold's release_evidence and target_binding.\nE4: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/blob/6d6f42226987f9ef9977f46dbb869455a88c25e2/reports/sprints/BOOK2-TARGET-AUTHORITY-REMEDIATION-1-owner-review-20260905.md;\nmeijer1973, 2026-09-05, book-2-ei-semantic-supersession, current semantic hash\n919c39f64dd212dba37b62902a5bb2e2ce6388c6020a0491e1621017ae2192a1.\nE5: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/pull/226#issuecomment-5521351557;\nmeijer1973, 2026-09-03. E5 is not approval to merge new textbook output.\n\n### Foundation verdict\n\nCurrent action: goal_design. Foundation verdict: PASS_FOR_GOAL_DESIGN.\nAll open holds are outside §2.1.1 or unrelated to this action. The separate\napproved paragraph_production probe also passes the foundation validator.\nNeither mechanical result is an independent plan or final production verdict.\nProduction state remains WAIT_FOR_INDEPENDENT_PARAGRAPH_PLAN_ACCEPTANCE.\nH-BOOK2-ROOT-PLAN blocks book_readiness/whole_book_assembly, not this paragraph;\nH-CHAPTER-23-PLAN and the elastic/retrieval holds must be resolved before their\nown affected actions. This paragraph neither releases nor waits on those holds.\n\n## Part A backward-design plan\n\n### Goals and target route\n\nUse these four frozen lesson_goals verbatim, numbered 1–4:\n\n1. Je kunt kostencomponenten als constant of variabel classificeren op basis van hun gedrag binnen een genoemde periode en bij gelijkblijvende productiecapaciteit.\n2. Je kunt uit een context de functies voor TCK, TVK en TK opstellen.\n3. Je kunt gemiddelde kosten berekenen en met de juiste eenheid interpreteren.\n4. Je kunt verklaren hoe totale en gemiddelde kosten veranderen als Q verandert, binnen de aannames van het model.\n\nThe source route is blueprint v5 §2.1.1 → frozen registry id 2.1.1 → exact\ntarget source/table/questions → these goals → worked example/support/independent\npractice → unchanged target. Exam codes D1.16, D1.17, A2.10 are curriculum\nalignment metadata, not an assertion that this is an official exam question.\nRequired/new skills are A08, A14, A50, A86, D38. The flagged D02 prerequisite of\nD38 is not imported: profit/MO=MK remain deferred. No registry normalization here.\n\n#### Frozen target and answer contract\n\nTarget number in this set: Opgave 7, with original a–e labels and 4/3/3/3/4\npoints (17 total). Generate the context, table, prompts and points directly\nfrom the pinned record, preserving wording and all empty response cells.\nDo not paraphrase the frozen question to fit a page.\n\nContext: Bakkerij De Korenaar produceert in één maand tussen 500 en 1.000 broden. Zolang de productiecapaciteit gelijk blijft, gebruikt de bakkerij dezelfde ruimte en ovens. Huur en verzekering kosten samen € 440 per maand. De netaansluiting en het energieabonnement kosten € 60 per maand. Meel en verpakking kosten samen € 0,70 per brood. Het elektriciteitsverbruik van de ovens kost binnen deze grenzen € 0,10 per brood. Q is het aantal broden per maand.\n\nSource id classificatietabel: columns **kostencomponent / soort kosten / reden**.\nFour rows, with the latter two cells empty: huur en verzekering;\nnetaansluiting en energieabonnement; meel en verpakking; elektriciteitsverbruik ovens.\nSource content: “Vul de lege cellen in.”\n\n| Label/points/time | Exact prompt | Planned answer evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| a / 4 / 2.5 min | Vul de classificatietabel in: classificeer elk onderdeel als constante of variabele kosten en noteer per onderdeel kort hoe het totale bedrag reageert op een verandering van Q. | First two constant because total monthly amount does not vary with Q; last two variable because total increases with each bread. Retain distinct energy subscription/usage rows |\n| b / 3 / 2 min | Stel de functies voor TCK, TVK en TK op. | TCK = 440 + 60 = 500; TVK = (0,70 + 0,10)Q = 0,80Q; TK = 500 + 0,80Q; all totals euro per month |\n| c / 3 / 1.5 min | Bereken bij Q = 500 de GCK, GVK en GTK. Noteer de volledige eenheden. | GCK = 500/500 = € 1,00 per brood; GVK = 400/500 = € 0,80 per brood; GTK = 900/500 = € 1,80 per brood |\n| d / 3 / 1.5 min | Bereken bij Q = 1.000 de GCK, GVK en GTK. Noteer de volledige eenheden. | GCK = 500/1.000 = € 0,50 per brood; GVK = 800/1.000 = € 0,80 per brood; GTK = 1.300/1.000 = € 1,30 per brood |\n| e / 4 / 4.5 min | Vergelijk eerst TCK, TVK en TK bij Q = 500 en Q = 1.000. Leg daarna met de uitkomsten uit waarom GCK halveert, GVK gelijk blijft en GTK niet halveert als Q verdubbelt. Begrens je uitleg tot één maand, Q = 500–1.000 en gelijkblijvende productiecapaciteit. | TCK 500→500, TVK 400→800, TK 900→1.300 euro per month. GCK 1,00→0,50: same fixed total spread over twice the quantity. GVK 0,80→0,80 only because its per-bread coefficient is constant here. GTK 1,80→1,30, not 0,90: only its fixed part halves. Explicit month/range/capacity conclusion |\n\nTarget time is planned at 12 minutes (the record says circa 11); the extra\nminute protects the four-component classification reasons and bounded\nthree-part explanation, without changing the immutable record's estimate.\nPoint subdivision of the expanded answer rubric remains subject to independent\nteacher review; the five approved totals cannot change.\n\n| Lesson goal | Target subquestion/operation | Worked example | Start check | Guided practice | Independent practice | Covered/gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1: behavior-based classification within period/capacity | a: classify four components and explain each total response to Q | Bicycle atelier: classify both fixed and both per-repair components with reasons, including month/range/capacity | 2a briefly checks two components and reasons; not the full four-row target | 3 classification table; 5 contract-change misconception | 6a, four blank classified rows with reasons | Covered in planned teaching, guided and independent practice; Start is deliberately partial, not attainment evidence |\n| 2: construct TCK, TVK and TK functions | b: combine fixed components and per-unit components separately into all three functions | Bicycle atelier: 180 + 20 = 200, (1 + 1)Q = 2Q, TK = 200 + 2Q; Q/domain/dimensions explained | No direct function-construction check; 1a,b retrieve substitution only and do not cover this new operation | 3 partially filled functions; 4 removes formula-selection hints | 6b supplies only context and asks all three functions | Covered by the fully modeled example and 3/4/6b; not assessed in Start by design, no hidden coverage claim |\n| 3: calculate and interpret averages with units | c,d: calculate all three averages at each of two quantities, with full units | Bicycle atelier: divide each total by the same positive Q; both numeric rows and euro/repair dimension | 2b briefly checks total/per-unit dimensions; 1c retrieves division/unit checking, not all six new average calculations | 3 shows one row; 4 removes intermediate arithmetic | 6c,d asks all six averages with units for two Q values | Covered in planned example/practice; Start samples units only and does not retest the target |\n| 4: explain total and average changes within assumptions | e: compare three totals, explain three average changes, and bound month/range/capacity | Bicycle atelier: all six comparisons, causal explanations, stated conditions and rejection of all-averages-halve claim | No direct full trend-explanation check; 2a touches component behavior only, not the six-quantity comparison | 4 comparison; 5 isolates fixed/variable changes then combines | 6e requires totals first, all three average explanations and bounded conclusion | Covered in planned example, guided comparison and independent 6e; full operation deliberately absent from brief Start, not a silent gap |\n\nTarget-equivalent independent evidence is Opgave 6, not Start completion,\nnot an image-reading check and not the guided route. All goals have a complete\npaper explanation and explanation-rich answers. None depends on a digital lesson.\n\n### Exercise, explanation, and worked-example sequence\n\n#### Explanation design and whole-lesson budget\n\nMotivation (2 min): a poster atelier asks whether twice as many posters means\ntwice as high a total bill and half the cost per poster. Do not answer by slogan.\nName the month, Q = 40–80 posters/month and unchanged capacity. Use fixed costs\n€ 120/month and variable materials € 2/poster consistently throughout theory.\n\nFormal instruction (12 min, four 3-minute blocks):\n\n1. Define constant/variable costs by response of the total to Q in this month/range; separate an energy subscription from usage. The invoice label is not the criterion.\n2. Build TCK = 120, TVK = 2Q, TK = 120 + 2Q step by step. At Q = 40 totals are 120, 80, 200 euro/month; at 80 they are 120, 160, 280. Table and staged total-cost figure encode those same numbers.\n3. Define GCK = TCK/Q, GVK = TVK/Q, GTK = TK/Q = GCK + GVK. Show the dimension (euro/month)/(posters/month) = euro/poster. At 40 averages are 3, 2, 5; at 80 they are 1,50, 2, 3,50 euro/poster.\n4. Explain each change causally and bind it to this model. Display average-cost comparison after establishing division; confront “all averages halve” and “GVK is always constant.” Do not introduce a formal curve taxonomy.\n\nEach definition gets one compact definition box; two formula boxes contain\nat most three relations each; validity conditions accompany the first formula.\nWarnings immediately follow the misconception they address. The economics\nprecision reference §§7.3–7.5 overrides a generic graph recipe demanding a\nU-shaped GTK: in this bounded linear model GTK decreases and GVK is constant.\n\nUitgewerkt voorbeeld (8 min): a bicycle repair atelier performs Q = 100–200\nrepairs in one month at unchanged capacity. Workspace rent € 180/month,\ninsurance € 20/month, cleaning materials € 1/repair and small parts € 1/repair.\nName Q as repairs/month. Explicitly demonstrate all five target stages:\nclassification/reasons; TCK = 200, TVK = 2Q, TK = 200 + 2Q; total rows\n(200,200,400) and (200,400,600); average rows (2,2,4) and (1,2,3)\neuro/repair; then constant/doubled/rising totals and three bounded average\nexplanations. Use a thought-aloud choice of numerator and unit check, not\nunexplained substitution. No new operation, graph construction or profit.\n\nCompact non-heading summary/transitions (2 min): maximum five points covering\nbehavior/conditions; total functions; average formulas/units; conditional\ndoubling comparison; forward pointer to §2.1.2 without teaching revenue now.\nPlace it directly after the worked example and before Startopgaven.\n\nStandard whole-lesson equation:\n2 motivation + 12 instruction + 8 example + 2 summary/transitions\n+ 6 Start + 12 independent + 12 target = **54 minutes**, with 1 minute reserve.\nEstimates cover reading, calculations and written explanations, not merely\nsilent arithmetic. They are planning estimates, not classroom observations.\nIndependent teacher review must challenge these concrete budgets.\n\nThe printed guided detour adds 12 minutes: supported completion is **66 minutes**\nbefore the reserve, not falsely advertised as ≤55. Teacher schedules that\nsupport before/after the core lesson or carries remaining independent/target\nwork into a further supervised period. Bonus adds 8 and closing retrieval 4\noutside core, normally homework or a later lesson; neither is a hidden compulsory\ncomponent of the 54-minute equation.\n\n#### Exact section order and question-level design\n\nStudent source uses these seven exact level-two headings, in order:\nUitgewerkt voorbeeld; Startopgaven; Begeleide inoefening; Zelfstandige oefening;\nDoeloefening; Denkertje / Bonusopgave; Herhaling / Herhaling en interleaving.\nThe compact summary is not another heading. Opgaven source carries the same\nexercise sequence and required worked support, without the preceding theory.\nOne canonical exercise source feeds both forms to prevent drift.\n\n**Startopgaven — Opgaven 1–2, 6 min total.**\nPrint: “Korte route: Startopgaven → Zelfstandige oefening → Doeloefening.\nExtra hulp nodig? Maak eerst Begeleide inoefening.”\n\n- 1 (3 min, A04 retrieval): A club uses the supplied arithmetic rule B = 30 + 2n, with B the material budget in euro and n the number of participants. (a, 1 min) Calculate B for n = 10: 50 euro. (b, 1 min) For n = 20: 70 euro. (c, 1 min) Divide the first budget by 10 and describe the unit: 5 euro per participant. Supply the brief order-of-operations reminder in the answer, not cost classification as an assumed prerequisite.\n- 2 (3 min, compact current-content check): A printer pays a € 40 monthly machine fee and € 0,50 paper per card, Q = 100–200 cards/month with unchanged capacity. (a, 1.5 min) Classify both components and explain their total response to Q. (b, 1.5 min) Choose euro/month or euro/card for TCK and GCK and explain the difference. Answers: fee constant, paper variable; total versus per-card amount. This checks just-taught material, not diagnostic attainment or automatic routing.\n\n**Begeleide inoefening — Opgaven 3–5, optional use, always printed; 12 min.**\nPrint: “Heb je deze hulp niet nodig? Ga dan verder met Zelfstandige oefening.”\nRetain the target's classification-table response form while fading labels,\nexample rows, formula cues and intermediate steps. No invented graph-production\nfading requirement.\n\n- 3 (4 min, strongest support): badge workshop, one month, Q = 50–100 badges, same capacity; rent € 120/month, insurance € 30/month, metal € 0,50/badge, pin € 0,50/badge. (a, 1 min) Read a table with rent already classified constant and its reason; complete the other three rows. (b, 1 min) Complete TCK = 120 + …, TVK = (… + …)Q, TK = … + …. (c, 2 min) Given total and average rows at Q = 50, complete the Q = 100 row and one “because” sentence. Expected functions 150, Q, 150 + Q; totals (150,50,200)/(150,100,250); averages (3,1,4)/(1,50,1,2,50) euro/badge. The filled model row is clearly worked support, not disguised assessment.\n- 4 (3 min, reduced support): bookmark atelier, one month, Q = 40–80 bookmarks, fixed fee € 80/month, paper € 2/bookmark, same capacity. (a, 1 min) Write three total functions without formula blanks. (b, 1 min) Complete a table with only headings Q/GCK/GVK/GTK. (c, 1 min) Compare totals and explain why GTK changes from 4 to 3, not to 2 euro/bookmark. Answers: 80, 2Q, 80 + 2Q; totals (80,80,160)/(80,160,240), averages (2,2,4)/(1,2,3). Only table headings remain; the answer gives full reasoning.\n- 5 (5 min, last guid