nt21 reproduction and\nown answer7 view plus30 exact prior page views are separately rebound by346 checks\nin `reports/sprints/BOOK2-TEXTBOOK-PRODUCTION-1-211-root-qc-bindings-r5.json`.\nNeither immutable generation evidence nor historical approval is rewritten.\n\nPublisher-print validation and page review accept this paragraph only. Chapter\nassembly must use its complete paragraaf once and must not append the duplicate\nopgaven route. Answers remain a separate edition. No chapter/book has passed yet.\n\n## 3. Target exercise and operation chain\n\n- Target: printed Opgave 7, Bakkerij De Korenaar, exactly 17 points (4/3/3/3/4).\n- Frozen record: `143f1053c98766b77d9d9ce573a5c8e976980f900387159312c3238288d71710`.\n- Registry status stays `candidate_review_ready`; separate integrated lifecycle\n  authority, not a renamed status, permits scoped production.\n- Required operations: classify four components with behavioral reasons;\n  form TCK/TVK/TK; compute GCK/GVK/GTK at Q = 500 and 1,000 with units;\n  compare all three totals and explain all three average changes.\n- Required source use: fill the supplied four-row classification table's\n  eight blank classification/reason cells. No graph construction is required.\n- Required answer form: justified table, three functions, two average-cost\n  rows with units, and bounded total/average explanations.\n- Prior knowledge: A04 substitution and elementary division/unit checking,\n  retrieved in print. Formal cost classification and dimensions are new.\n- Boundary: one month, Q = 500–1,000, unchanged capacity. Do not extrapolate.\n\n## 4. Concepts and terminology\n\n| Concept | Student-facing meaning | Formula | Canonical term / avoid |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Constant cost | Total amount does not change with Q within stated period/capacity | TCK | constante kosten; not simply 'a bill paid monthly' |\n| Variable cost | Total amount changes with Q under the chosen contract | TVK = vQ in this model | variabele kosten; not every changed contract price |\n| Total cost | Constant plus variable total for the same period | TK = TCK + TVK | totale kosten; not an average |\n| Average constant cost | Matching fixed total per product | GCK = TCK/Q | gemiddelde constante kosten; not another invoice |\n| Average variable cost | Matching variable total per product | GVK = TVK/Q | gemiddelde variabele kosten; not universally constant |\n| Average total cost | Matching total cost per product | GTK = TK/Q = GCK + GVK | gemiddelde totale kosten; does not generally halve |\n\nTotals use euro per month here; averages use euro per named product. Q is\npositive when dividing. 'Constant' classifies behavior against Q, not across\ndifferent contracts. A fixed variable cost per product is an explicit model\nassumption, never an unrestricted economic law.\n\n## 5. Procedures\n\n| Procedure | Registry mapping | Bounded steps taught here | Printed location |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Classify component behavior | New contextual cost classification | Fix period/range/capacity; vary Q conceptually; state how total amount responds | Theory, bicycle model, 2–7 |\n| Construct totals | A08/A86 | Sum fixed components; sum per-product variable amounts; multiply by Q; combine and check units | Theory, worked steps 1–2, 3/4/6/7 |\n| Compute averages | A14/A50 | Select matching total, divide by the same positive Q, state per-product unit, verify sum | Theory, worked steps 3–4, 3/4/6/7 |\n| Explain changes | D38, bounded without D02 | Compare totals first; connect numerator/Q changes; distinguish GCK/GVK/GTK and preserve assumptions | Worked step 5, 4/5/6/7/8 |\n\nThese are paragraph-scoped uses of the registry mappings, not permission to\nimport each machine unit's entire procedure. In particular, do not import\nquadratic cost/U-shape teaching, Q = 0 extrapolation, marginal-cost assumptions,\nD02 profit optimization or MO = MK from broader machine prerequisites.\n\n## 6. Core visuals\n\nEvery listed base has both SVG and PNG under `_assets/`.\n\n| Base | Concept / printed use | Later reuse guidance |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2.1.1_fig_1 | Total-to-average numerator map in theory | Preserve different units and matching Q |\n| 2.1.1_fig_2 | TCK-only first graph | Keep period/range and introduce only one relation |\n| 2.1.1_fig_3 | TVK panel, then TK added with identical axes | Retain equal scales and explicit difference |\n| 2.1.1_fig_4 | GCK/GVK/GTK at two production levels | Preserve reasons, not only numerical patterns |\n| 2.1.1_we_1 | Bicycle totals and averages | Keep worked quantities/units consistent |\n| 2.1.1_ex_1 | Guided badge classification and division cue | Support must fade before independent work |\n\nAll current text is at least 12 pt in print, with placed figure labels above\n13 pt. Orange-stroke contrast is a bounded enhancement flag: equivalent dark\nvisible information conveys every required relation here. Essential curve\nreading in future material requires a new contrast judgment, not this exception.\n\n## 7. Exercise map\n\n| Exercise | Operation | Answer location | Potential later support need |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Worked bicycle | Complete target chain at two Q levels | Printed worked steps 1–5 | Model selection and unit reasoning visibly |\n| 1a–c | A04 substitution/division retrieval | Answers, Startopgaven 1 | Old arithmetic support, not new cost diagnosis |\n| 2a–b | Brief classification/dimension comprehension | Answers 2 | Distinguish total response from average unit |\n| 3a–c | Guided classification/functions/two averages | Answers 3 | Filled first row then completion |\n| 4a–c | Faded functions, averages and causal comparison | Answers 4 | Remove supplied choices progressively |\n| 5a–d | Separate/combine contract effects, expose trap | Answers 5 | Distinguish changed contract from changed Q |\n| 6a–e | Independent complete sticker chain | Answers 6 | No supplied classification or average answers |\n| 7a–e | Exact frozen bakery target | Answers 7, full 17-point rubric | Preserve blank student cells and scoring |\n| 8a–c | Refute constant-GVK generalization, model limits | Answers 8 | Reason across cases, no new curve-name demand |\n| 9a–b | Cumulative substitution/per-participant retrieval | Answers 9 | Accessible closing, not new theory |\n\nBonus8 retains its complete original8a–c model followed by exactly three explicit\nassessment criteria: both GVK calculations/units, conditional generalization,\nand plausible explanation without fixed-cost confusion or a uniquely inferred\nfunction. No additional task or point allocation is introduced.\n\n## 8. Known boundaries\n\n- Part B may later reuse accepted terms, figures, procedure scope, exact frozen\n  target and source pins, subject to its own authorized lane and reviews.\n- It may adapt scaffolding/feedback for another medium, not claim paper review\n  has validated interactive behavior or student mastery.\n- It must not change targets, point allocation, Ei semantics, capacity/period\n  restrictions, answer ownership or machine prerequisites through this handoff.\n- No open core defect remains for this paragraph. Classroom timing is not\n  measured:54-minute core,66-minute supported route,78 minutes all printed work.\n  Written explanations make the core plausible but tight. Guided support and\n  bonus/closing need planned continuation time; this is not an all-learners\n  single-lesson completion or attainment guarantee.\n- Named follow-ups: observed pacing/attainment, contrast enhancement, separately\n  authorized Part B and protected external-reference refresh. Optional Inspectie\n  mapping was omitted rather than presented as current compliance.\n\n## 9. Companion start decision\n\n- Technical status: READY_FOR_COMPANION.\n- Reason: current independent R5 paragraph review, distinct specialist QC,\n  root acceptance, exact reproducible R5 files, both Part A profiles and complete\n  print evidence are present. This does not accept a chapter/book or claim current fullCI.