op. Noteer zowel de continue break-even-afzet als het eerste gehele aantal broden waarbij geen verlies ontstaat. | 3 | 1,50Q=500+0,80Q → 0,70Q=500 (1); Q=714,2857… ≈714,29 continuous (1); first whole 715, checked profit €0,50 (1) | Frozen registry 2.1.2/c |\n| d | Teken TK en TO in één assenstelsel. Benoem beide assen met grootheid en eenheid, markeer het break-evenpunt en de winst- en verlieszone en geef bij Q=1.000 de winst van €200 weer als verticale afstand. Kleur geen oppervlakte als winst. | 4 | Correct named/unit axes (1); TK intercept500/slope0,80 and TO origin/slope1,50 (1); BE(714,29;1.071,43) with loss left/profit right (1); Q1.000 vertical 1.500−1.300=€200, no profit area (1) | Frozen registry 2.1.2/d |\n\nTotal = 2+2+3+4 = **11 points**. The point distribution above operationalizes\nthe frozen short answer model; no extra mandatory operation is smuggled in.\nScale/line plotting serve d; a separate pupil-produced table is not demanded.\nA small self-made plotting table is an optional method. This is an authored\ncurriculum target, not an official CvTE question: no fabricated exam year,\nquestion number, official source annex or official correction model. All\nneeded source information is the supplied context/functions. Registry exam\ncodes A2.1/A2.10/A2.14/D1.14/D1.19/D1.20 remain source metadata, not claims of\nofficial-exam provenance. Required skills A07/A08/A21 and reported missing\nunits are retained diagnostically; this plan does not create machine units.\n\n#### Required backward-alignment table\n\nWE is the fully worked kayak case below; G3/G4 are optional guided exercises;\nI6 is unsupported independent minigolf practice; T7 is the frozen target.\nStart checks are low-stakes comprehension/retrieval, not mastery or routing.\n\n| Lesson goal | Target subquestion/operation | Worked example | Start check | Guided practice | Independent practice | Covered/gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1: TO function | a: multiply constant unit price by Q | 