ofit|\n|Guided5|Separate/combine price and fixed costs; answers5|One-factor change before combination|\n|Independent6|Minigolf full calculation and self-built graph; answers6|No supplied final graph or target answer|\n|Target7a–d|Exact bakery chain and11-point rubric; answers7|All parts and graph workload remain required|\n|Bonus8|Two evaluative scale questions; answers8 with exactly3 criteria|Same€30 gap atQ30 despite different paper lengths|\n|Closing9|Cumulative totals/GTK; answers9|Earlier costs only; no new goal|\n\n## 8. Retained flags and downstream boundaries\n\nTiming54 core/67 supported/77 all is **UNOBSERVED**. Complete core includes both\nindependent graph tasks and only one spare minute. Named follow-up is classroom\nobservation of component times, student work and support needs; do not remove\nrequired operations to obtain an estimate. Bonus6 and closing4 are outside core.\n212-R5-RECAP remains nonblocking: body/answers qualify model/range/increasing\nprofit, but recap does not repeat every condition. Any improvement requires\nauthorized source regeneration and renewed exact-output review, not silent edits.\n212-QC-INSPECTIE-FRESHNESS remains nonblocking: optional mapping omitted; a\nprotected-reference refresh/compliance judgment is separately authorized work.\n\nOld specialist failures and native PENDING manifests are preserved, not erased\nby current acceptance. Legacy header/unchanged historical QC wording is not new\ncurrent acceptance. Only explicit root fields and this nine-section handoff are\nrenewed. No PartB/exit-ticket/PPTX, observed attainment, PDF-UA/AT certification,\nchapter/book acceptance, current fullCI or future merge grant is implied.\nH-213-OPC2 remains open and outside the agreed interval-change scope.\n\n## 9. Companion start decision and current continuation\n\n**READY_FOR_COMPANION as an accepted source boundary only; NOT_COMMISSIONED.**\nPart A source, independent reviews, native reproduction and paragraph gates pass;\nthis i