agraph 2.1.3`: PASS |\n| Durable target invariant | `node build-scripts/workflows/check-book2-target-authority-remediation.js --durable`: PASS |\n| Explicit non-goal boundary probe | Currentness `--require-approved --action formal_output_choice_teaching --paragraph 2.1.3`: expected FAIL, H-213-OPC2 remains blocking for that different action |\n\nTask grant is the separate owner authorization at platform\n`6e35f4fe0aeaa448da9476469294ccd45775232d`, not the content-only decision at\n`6d6f42226987f9ef9977f46dbb869455a88c25e2`. Activation is\n`206c018478654db781cc879e7ea36adcd9ef600c`; PR #231 merged at\n`96416b6b5bd57094576e9aba0a42d682584ec479`. Parent evidence records green main\nCI run `33963305398`; this builder does not claim to have rerun it. There is no\nfuture-PR merge authorization. No goal, target, Ei rule or historical approval\nis changed, and no status is promoted to `reviewed_final`.\n\n### Canonical paragraph semantics\n\n| Required semantic decision | Paragraph-specific value/evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Paragraph role | Define and calculate MK=ΔTK/ΔQ and MO=ΔTO/ΔQ over stated table intervals; compare linear/nonlinear total-cost patterns without derivatives; outline §2.1.3 |\n| Chapter dependency | §2.1.1 total/average costs, then §2.1.2 total revenue/profit and vertical profit difference, then §2.1.3 intervals, then §2.1.4 consolidation |\n| Incoming prerequisites | Read Q/TK/TO at matching rows; substitute in a supplied total function; subtract same-period monetary totals, including a negative result; divide a quantity by its matching positive count; distinguish totals and per-product amounts |\n| Prerequisite classification | §211 cost/substitution/average-unit operations: `previously_taught_retrieval_required`. §212 TO and signed profit: intended `previously_taught_retrieval_required` in delivery order, but currently `previously_taught_not_secure_enough_to_assume` as an unaccepted-output dependency. Book1 supplied-cost/profit familiarity: `preview_or_familiarity_only`. MK/MO interval normalization, right-endpoint notation and bounded interval pattern interpretation: `new_formal_learning`. Nothing is classified as probably secure merely from a registry ID |\n| Classification evidence/support | Renewed §211 R3 source and accepted handoff are in this base; §212 is read as a plan only. Production may not claim “In §2.1.2 leerde je…” until root supplies its accepted teaching/handoff. Print a short worked retrieval box before dependent use and Start1 retrieval; guided support remains on paper. No learner mastery is inferred |\n| Explicit non-goals | Formal output-choice teaching, a profit-maximizing Q, MO=MK as a choice rule, derivatives/instantaneous marginals, differentiating Q², market structures, supply-as-MC teaching, elasticity/surplus, new total-cost curve classifications or machine-unit repair |\n| Downstream prepares-for | §2.1.4 observed profit-growth comparison; later §2.3.2 supply-as-MC bridge and later firm analysis, without teaching those later formal procedures now |\n| Retrieval | Only totals, subtraction, division, units and row reading that the target and worked example use; no break-even solving or new pupil graph construction |\n| Interleaving | Profit column from §212 and total-versus-average unit distinction from §211; approved C21 bounded Δprofit explanation connects to the vertical profit distance, not an output recommendation |\n| Operation emphasis | Complete supplied tables; show both interval differences and divide by ΔQ; place the interval result at its right endpoint; compare constant/rising patterns; explain per-extra-product meaning within that interval |\n| Misconception boundary | A row difference is not automatically a per-product marginal; MK is not TK/Q; the right endpoint is a display convention, not the cost of that endpoint's single product; fixed-price MO is constant only under that assumption; an observed profit increase is not an optimal-output proof |\n| Model conditions/relevant range | One enterprise, one stated period and supplied production/sales range per practice case; Q produced equals Q sold; compare matching totals from the same case and period; ΔQ>0. Q0 totals are legal but no marginal exists in the first row without a preceding interval. Conclusions refer to the stated interval, not its unobserved internal units or extrapolated quantities |\n\nExact prerequisite evidence pins:\n\n- §211 `2.1.1-textbook-handoff.md`, full chapter-relative path\n  `2.1.1 Kostenstructuren/2.1.1-textbook-handoff.md`, LF hash\n  `724a080619f2f072151edf20980071b3bef18cd60d1904c78f4aa906be8917c8`.\n  Its reviewed lesson source is `c37dfba8c68cbe86b3b12534e020fda6e2481ac5`,\n  integrated review/quality head `60ad41b555d26b12ba74e9df3014e920bcf99264`.\n  It actually teaches TK and total/average distinctions, not revenue or profit.\n- §212 chapter-relative path\n  `2.1.2 Opbrengsten, winst en break-even/2.1.2-textbook-plan.md`, version\n  `BOOK2-TEXTBOOK-PRODUCTION-1-212-plan-v1`, LF hash\n  `5e1d318dd1b841467ca297d67956304d1861e3eb68d1df56cc4d32f6434d34a4`.\n  The planned theatre/kayak route explicitly teaches TO, signed profit and\n  same-Q vertical monetary distance. No legacy §212 output or verdict was\n  treated as accepted evidence. This dependency pin must be supplemented by\n  the actually accepted handoff before §213 production release.\n\nThe registry's A07/A08/A21 mappings are bounded by this chain. A07's broader\ninverse-demand/monopoly procedure is not imported; A08 does not authorize\nquadratic-cost classification or unrestricted Q0 extrapolation; A21 supplies\nTO−TK at the same Q, not maximization. Supplied Q² totals are already printed;\nthe pupil subtracts their values, never differentiates them. Historical outline\nreadiness/audit snapshots are not substitutes for current holds or reviewed\nplans, and their historical text is not repaired here.\n\n### Open holds and current-action effect\n\nExact evidence aliases:\n\n- E1: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/pull/226#issuecomment-5515033629\n- E2: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/pull/227#issuecomment-5524345692\n- E3: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/blob/6e35f4fe0aeaa448da9476469294ccd45775232d/reports/sprints/BOOK2-TARGET-INTEGRATION-1-owner-authorization.md\n- E4: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/blob/6d6f42226987f9ef9977f46dbb869455a88c25e2/reports/sprints/BOOK2-TARGET-AUTHORITY-REMEDIATION-1-owner-review-20260905.md\n- E5-root: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/blob/77288fcbf6eddd58779052b66c97227076e1fcd9/reports/sprints/BOOK2-TEXTBOOK-PRODUCTION-1-root-plan-review.md\n- E5-23: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/blob/77288fcbf6eddd58779052b66c97227076e1fcd9/reports/sprints/BOOK2-TEXTBOOK-PRODUCTION-1-chapter-23-plan-review.md\n- E6: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/blob/26a330cd1b3a306a801366d119a64474eb7782ed/reports/sprints/BOOK2-TEXTBOOK-PRODUCTION-1-22-owner-authorization.md\n- E7: https://github.com/meijer1973/4veco-platform/pull/226#issuecomment-5521351557\n\nAll22 holds are accounted for, with action membership evaluated exactly for\n`goal_design`. Released rows remain RELEASED even when their scope is unrelated.\n\n| Hold ID | Status | Scope match? | Current action | Listed in blocks? | Listed in permits? | Listed as resolution action? | Effect | Release evidence when released |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| H-OUTLINE-OWNER | released | yes, book2 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E1 |\n| H-211-GATE0B1 | released | no, §211 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E2 |\n| H-211-TARGET-INTEGRATION | released | no, §211 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E2 |\n| H-229-211-CANDIDATE | released | no, §211 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.1.1 |\n| H-212-STALE-REF | released | no, §212 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.1.2 |\n| H-213-DELTAQ | released | yes, §213 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, exact §213 record pin above, integrated206c018 |\n| H-229-214-CANDIDATE | released | no, §214 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.1.4 |\n| H-229-221-CANDIDATE | released | no, §221 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.2.1 |\n| H-229-222-CANDIDATE | released | no, §222 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.2.2 |\n| H-229-223-CANDIDATE | released | no, §223 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.2.3 |\n| H-229-224-CANDIDATE | released | no, §224 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.2.4 |\n| H-231-V5 | released | no, §231 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.3.1 |\n| H-232-V5 | released | no, §232 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.3.2 |\n| H-233-V5-REF | released | no, §233 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.3.3 |\n| H-234-PLACEHOLDER | released | no, §234 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E3, subject2.3.4 |\n| H-213-OPC2 | open | yes, paragraph2.1.3; formal extension remains outside task | goal_design | no | yes | no | PERMITS | null; blocks formal_output_choice_teaching only, resolution target_authority_repair not performed |\n| H-221-PRIOR | released | no, §221 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E6 |\n| H-22-ELASTIC-CONTRAST | released | no, §§221–222 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E6 |\n| H-229-EI-SUPERSESSION | released | no, §223 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E4 |\n| H-BOOK2-ROOT-PLAN | released | yes, book2 | goal_design | no | no | no | RELEASED | E5-root |\n| H-CHAPTER-23-PLAN | released | no, chapter2.3 | goal_design | no | yes | no | RELEASED | E5-23 |\n| H-MERGE-GOVERNANCE | released | yes, book2 | goal_design | no | no | no | RELEASED | E7, historical PR226 only |\n\n### Foundation verdict\n\nCurrent action: `goal_design` (planning how to teach already frozen goals,\nnot changing their authority or wording).\nFoundation verdict: `PASS_FOR_GOAL_DESIGN`.\nH-213-OPC2 explicitly permits this action and remains open; it blocks the\ndifferent, out-of-project action `formal_output_choice_teaching`. No target\nhold blocks this plan. This foundation result is not independent plan review,\nteacher/economics acceptance, §212 prerequisite acceptance or production release.\n\n## Part A backward-design plan\n\n### Goals and target route\n\nAll four frozen goals, verbatim; no fifth terminal goal:\n\n1. Je kunt MK als ΔTK/ΔQ en MO als ΔTO/ΔQ over een tabelinterval berekenen.\n2. Je kunt gegeven totale kosten en totale opbrengsten gebruiken om een winstkolom in te vullen.\n3. Je kunt constante en stijgende marginale patronen vergelijken zonder afgeleiden.\n4. Je kunt uitleggen wat MK en MO per extra product binnen het genoemde tabelinterval betekenen.\n\n#### Exact frozen target and actual sources\n\n> Onderneming Linea heeft TK = 200 + 3Q en TO = 8Q. Onderneming Curva heeft TK = 100 + Q² en verkoopt ieder product voor € 30, zodat TO = 30Q. Bedragen zijn in euro. Bereken marginale waarden per extra product over ieder tabelinterval: MK = ΔTK/ΔQ en MO = ΔTO/ΔQ. Gebruik geen afgeleiden.\n\nSource `tabel-linea`, type `table`; retain these six exact columns and cells.\nEmpty cells below are genuinely blank pupil cells, not zero or answer hints.\n\n| Q | TK | TO | winst | MK | MO |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | €200 | €0 | | — | — |\n| 10 | €230 | €80 | | | |\n| 20 | €260 | €160 | | | |\n| 30 | €290 | €240 | | | |\n\nVul de lege cellen in. Noteer een intervalwaarde voor MK en MO steeds bij het rechter eindpunt.\n\nSource `tabel-curva`, type `table`; preserve the supplied profit column.\n\n| Q | TK | TO | winst | MK | MO |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | €100 | €0 | −€100 | — | — |\n| 5 | €125 | €150 | €25 | | |\n| 10 | €200 | €300 | €100 | | |\n| 15 | €325 | €450 | €125 | | |\n\nVul de lege cellen in. Noteer een intervalwaarde voor MK en MO steeds bij het rechter eindpunt.\n\nStudent source inventory: Linea10 blanks (four profit, three MK, three MO),\nCurva6 blanks (three MK, three MO); both Q0 rows retain two em dashes. Do not\nblank Curva profit or require new total-column construction. Native accessible\ntables are the actual source, not decorative table images. No graph construction\nis requested anywhere in the frozen target.\n\n| Part | Exact prompt | Points | Required answer / planned point allocation |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| a | Vul in de tabel van Linea de winstkolom in. | 4 | −€200,−€150,−€100,−€50 at Q0/10/20/30; one point per correct signed profit cell |\n| b | Bereken voor Linea MK en MO over het eerste interval. Laat teller en noemer zien en vul dezelfde intervalwaarden in bij de rechter eindpunten Q=10, Q=20 en Q=30. | 3 | MK=(230−200)/(10−0)=€3 per product (1); MO=(80−0)/(10−0)=€8 per product (1); both values correctly repeated at all three right endpoints with appropriate units (1) |\n| c | Leg uit waarom MO bij Linea constant is. | 2 | Fixed sale price€8 (1), so each extra product adds the same€8 revenue and every interval ratio is€8 per product (1); constant MK is not the cause of constant MO |\n| d | Bereken voor Curva MK over de drie intervallen en MO over het eerste interval. Vul de berekende MK- en MO-waarden in bij de juiste rechter eindpunten Q=5, Q=10 en Q=15. | 4 | MK=(125−100)/5=5, (200−125)/5=15, (325−200)/5=25 €/product at Q5/10/15 (one point each, correct interval and placement); MO=(150−0)/5=30 €/product and repeated at all three right endpoints (1) |\n| e | Vergelijk het MK-patroon van Linea en Curva en leg uit wat MK en MO per extra product binnen een tabelinterval betekenen. Trek geen conclusie over de winstmaximaliserende afzet. | 2 | Linea MK constant3 versus Curva increasing5/15/25 (1); both correct bounded meanings: average extra total cost/revenue per additional product over the interval (1). Do not replace this by TK/Q, TO/Q or single-unit endpoint claims |\n\nTotal: 4+3+2+4+2=15 points. Source trace is the exact registry `2.1.3` record,\nits two source IDs and five labelled subquestions, with historical detailed-v5\n§2.1.3 provenance. This is an authored curriculum target, not an official CvTE\nexam: no invented exam year, question number, official annex or correction\nmodel. A2.1/D1.14/D1.17/D1.19 remain metadata, not official-source claims.\nMissing dedicated interval/pattern machine units remain diagnostic; this plan\ndoes not create units or route students to unproduced digital support.\n\n#### Required seven-column operation alignment\n\nWE is the fully worked two-workshop example below; S1/S2 are Start items,\nG3–G5 optional guided items, I6 unsupported practice and T7 the unchanged target.\n“Planned” means design coverage only; no student output or mastery is accepted.\n\n| Lesson goal | Target subquestion/operation | Worked example | Start check | Guided practice | Independent practice | Covered/gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1: interval MK | b/d: subtract TK endpoints, divide by same positive ΔQ, including nonunit intervals | WE2 first interval(16−12)/(2−0)=2; WE4 rising2/6/10 | S2a distinguishes ΔTK8 from MK4 over ΔQ2 | G3 supplied numerator/denominator then completion; G4 unequal ΔQ2/4 with only first row solved | I6b/d full ratios for ΔQ4 with no worked row/hints | Planned, explicit→reduced→unsupported; production pending |\n| 1: interval MO | b/d: subtract TO endpoints and divide; repeat where constant price justifies it | WE2 (12−0)/2=6; WE4 MO12 | S2c interprets MO6, not total24 | G3 MO=(30−15)/(6−3); G4 no fraction template for last interval | I6b/d MO5 and24 without prompts | Planned; price assumption stated, not a universal law |\n| 1 and4: source placement | b/d: record interval results at right endpoints; first row dashes | WE tables label0–2 result at Q2, then2–4 atQ4 | S2a result atQ4 names interval2–4 | G3 interval arrows; G4 only plain source table | I6b/d all right endpoints, no arrows | Planned; no demand for pupil graph/table creation beyond filling supplied cells |\n| 2: signed profit | a: use same-row TO−TK for four cells | WE1 Lus−12/−4/4/12, all shown; Bout column supplied | S1c profit20−26=−6; S2 profits supplied for brief bridge | G3 first row worked then two completions; G4 only first profit supplied | I6a Draad four profit blanks, Kaft already given | Planned; accepted §212 teaching/handoff still required before production |\n| 3: compare patterns | c/e: constant MK vs rising interval MK, conditional constant MO | WE3 fixedP6 explains MO6; WE5 compares Lus2/2/2 to Bout2/6/10 | S2c relates same MO to unequal observed profit increases | G4 compare its2/6 with G3's2/2; G5 checks constant fee vs marginal change | I6c/e fixedP explanation and MK1/1/1 versus4/12/20 | Planned; no derivative/optimization operation |\n| 4: bounded meanings | e: cost/revenue per extra product within a named interval, not average over all Q | WE5 states both meanings and why endpoint is not one product's actual cost | S2a raw difference trap; S2c verbal MO meaning | G3 sentence stem; G4 uncued short explanation and no interval extrapolation | I6e explain both with €/product and stated interval | Planned; actual print, answer and independent review pending |\n\nApproved chapter bridge is **explanatory scaffolding**, not a fifth goal or\nextra target part: after recalling §212's vertical profit distance, demonstrate\nΔwinst=ΔTO−ΔTK and Δwinst/ΔQ=MO−MK over the **same** interval. Two theory\nintervals and one short faded S2 comparison supply the reviewed C21 requirement.\nIt replaces repetitive core marginal drills inside the timing equation below;\nit is not deferred solely to an optional route or used to choose an output.\n\n### Exercise, explanation, and worked-example sequence\n\n#### Theory, retrieval and mathematical conditions\n\nOpen with a photo-holder workshop comparing batches of ten additional holders:\n“Tien extra fotohouders kosten eerst €30 extra, daarna €50. Wat kost één extra\nfotohouder gemiddeld binnen elk van die twee stappen?” One day, Q0/10/20 holders\nmade and sold, fixed sale price€8 per holder. Only these supplied totals and\nintervals are used: TK20/50/100, TO0/80/160, profit−20/30/60. No total-cost\nformula or claim about unobserved quantities is introduced.\n\nBefore dependent use, a printed recall box demonstrates same-row TO−TK, reading\ntwo endpoints, ordinary subtraction/division and total-versus-per-item units.\nIt explicitly connects to accepted §211/§212 content only after that dependency\ngate closes. The box contains the necessary reminders on paper, not “look it\nup online” or assumed prior mastery.\n\n| Step | New teaching move and representation | Exact anchor / boundary |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Define interval and Δ as end minus start. Same table rows, first only Q and TK; verbal two-batch problem beside the table | 0–10 and10–20, ΔQ10 in both. fig1 then fig2 adds ΔTK30/50 and MK3/5 |\n| 2 | Definition box: interval MK is extra total cost divided by extra products. Show full fraction, units and right-endpoint placement; compare with GTK | First MK30/10=3 €/holder, not ΔTK30 and not TK50/Q10=5. AtQ10 display3 for0–10, not a statement about the tenth holder alone |\n| 3 | Add only the corresponding revenue information and define MO by the same interval structure | TO0/80/160; MO80/10=8 in both intervals because P8 fixed; fig3, same rows/layout as before |\n| 4 | Explain constant versus rising marginal patterns using normalized values, not raw total heights | MK3→5, MO8→8 over these two intervals. No calculus, smooth marginal curve, tangent or new curve classification |\n| 5 | Reconnect to §212: same-Q profit is the signed vertical difference TO−TK; compare changes in that difference | Profit−20→30→60, hence changes50 then30. fig4 shows(80−30)/10=5 and(80−50)/10=3 €/extra holder. Derive bounded identity by subtracting the two same-Q profits; no output recommendation |\n\nThis staged table/interval diagram is dual coding with algebra, numbers and\nwords; it does not make drawing a graph a pupil operation. Definitions explicitly\nsay interval averages of **additional totals**, distinct from averages of all\nproduction. ΔQ is positive even when an interval starts atQ0. A first-row dash\nmeans “no preceding interval”, not zero marginal cost/revenue.\n\nMisconception box pairs wrong and corrected reasoning, explaining the temptation:\nadjacent printed rows may look like adjacent products, but ΔQ can be2,4,5,10;\ntwo totals are compared, not divided by the ending Q. “€30 extra kosten dus\nMK€30” becomes “€30 voor10 extra producten, dus€3 per product over0–10”.\n“MK bijQ10 is de rekening voor product10” becomes “de waarde hoort bij het\ninterval0–10”. Fixed unit price explains constant MO, not constant MK. Even a\nlarger observed profit does not authorize extrapolation or an optimal-Q claim.\n\n#### Exact printed structure and question-level route\n\nBoth future combined paragraph and exercise derivative use these seven exact\nlevel-two headings, in order. Theory flows directly to WE, then a compact\nnon-heading recap, then Start. WE is unnumbered; exercises are1–9.\n\n1. `## Uitgewerkt voorbeeld`\n2. `## Startopgaven`\n3. `## Begeleide inoefening`\n4. `## Zelfstandige oefening`\n5. `## Doeloefening`\n6. `## Denkertje / Bonusopgave`\n7. `## Herhaling / Herhaling en interleaving`\n\n| Item | Exact planned source, task chain and answer anchors | Support / estimated time |\n|---|---|---|\n| WE1–5 | Two key-ring workshops, one day, Q0/2/4/6. Lus: TK=12+2Q, TO=6Q; supplied totals12/16/20/24 and0/12/24/36, solve profits−12/−4/4/12. Compute first MK2/MO6 with both differences; fill atQ2/4/6; explain constant MO from price6. Bout: TK=8+Q², TO=12Q; supplied totals8/12/24/44 and0/24/48/72, profits−8/12/24/28 already printed. Show MK2/6/10 and MO12 atQ2/4/6. Compare patterns and explain both interval meanings. Do not require evaluating Q² or any operation beyond target chain | Fully solved, two simpler tables with same target blank-pattern logic before demonstration; we1;8min |\n| Recap | At most five short points: interval endpoints/ΔQ; MK/MO fractions and units; profit from matching total cells; conditional constant MO versus MK pattern plus endpoint meaning; bounded Δprofit identity and forward reference to §214. Brief self-check against the four goals | Non-heading box immediately after WE; part of2min transitions |\n| Start1 retrieval | Reusable drink cups, one event, Q0–10, TK=18+2Q, TO=5Q supplied. a atQ4 computeTK26 andTO20; b GTK26/4=6.50 €/cup and distinguish units; c signed profit20−26=−6€ for the event. No MK introduced as prior knowledge | Printed §211/§212 retrieval,3min |\n| Start2 comprehension and faded bridge | Sports bottles, one day, fixedP6, supplied Q0/2/4, TK8/12/20, TO0/12/24, profits−8/0/4. a second interval: critique MK8, calculate8/2=4 and place atQ4 for2–4; b first profit-growth calculation is shown:(12−4)/2=4, complete the second:(…−…)/…=… →(12−8)/2=2 €/extra bottle; c explain MO6 and why equal extra revenue accompanies smaller profit growth in the second interval as MK rises2→4 | Brief low-stakes current-content check, one faded comparison as C21 requires; no score-based route/diagnosis/mastery;4min |\n| Guided3 | Fabric patches/day, Q0/3/6, TK9/15/21, TO0/15/30, fixedP5. Supply first profit−9 and full first interval fractionsMK(15−9)/(3−0)=2, MO(15−0)/(3−0)=5. a fill profits0/9; b complete last displayed fractions with missing numbers and recordMK2/MO5 atQ6; c complete short explanation stems for constant MO and each interval meaning | Explicit support, first row and arrows in ex1;4min |\n| Guided4 | Ceramic coasters/day, supplied Q0/2/6, TK10/14/38, TO0/16/48, fixedP8. Only first profit−10 and first marginal rowMK2/MO8 atQ2 given. a fill profits2/10; b calculate second MK(38−14)/(6−2)=6, MO(48−16)/(6−2)=8 and put atQ6; c compare itsMK2→6 with G3 constantMK2, explain fixed-price MO and both meanings over2–6 | Reduced support: plain table, no arrows/fraction or sentence templates; different ΔQ2 then4 deliberately matters;4min |\n| Guided5 combined change | Desk organizers/day, fixed comparison intervalQ2→6. BaselineTK14→22, TO12→36. A adds a€10 fixed fee to BOTH cost endpoints:TK24→32, TO unchanged. B changes price6→7:TO14→42, TK baseline unchanged. Both:TK24→32, TO14→42. a onlyA computeMK2, explain no change; b onlyB computeMO7 versus6; c both computeMK2/MO7 and profit atQ6=42−32=10; d refute “beide totalen stijgen, dus MK en MO stijgen allebei” because the fixed addition cancels from ΔTK | Last optional guided item; table supplies all scenario endpoints, pupils keep cost/revenue lenses separate then combine;4min |\n| Independent6 | Two notebook workshops/day, Q0/4/8/12, all totals supplied. DraadTK=20+Q:20/24/28/32, TO=5Q:0/20/40/60, all four profit cells blank, all six marginal cells blank. KaftTK=12+Q²:12/28/76/156, TO=24Q:0/96/192/288, profit−12/68/116/132 given, six marginals blank. a Draad profits−20/−4/12/28; b first interval fractionsMK1/MO5 and all endpoints; c fixedP5 explains MO5; d KaftMK4/12/20 and MO24 from first interval, fill endpoints; e compare both MK patterns and explain interval meanings without choosing an output | Target-equivalent supplied tables only, first-row dashes, no worked row, arrows, sentence stem or intermediate fraction;10min(2+2+1+3+2) |\n| Target7 | Exact Linea/Curva context, real tables, blank pattern, a–e and15points above. Target itself retains its authored Δ formula reminder; add no builder scaffold or answer leakage |12min(2+3+1+4+2), no target reduction |\n| Bonus8 | Optional packaging firms K/L, one day, Q0/4/12. K TK20/32/56; L TK20/40/56. a critique “bij K is de tweede kostenstijging groter, dus de MK ook”:12/4=3 versus24/8=3. b compare with L:20/4=5 versus16/8=2; same ending total56 does not imply the same interval pattern. c can these tables determine the separate cost of product5? No, interval totals do not identify individual internal increments; explain what extra information would be neede