rieve accepted211/212:\nsame-period totals, substitution, positive-Q average cost, revenue and signed\nprofit. Old plan wording about unaccepted212 is historical dependency state;\nactual current succession is closed by independent S1 review and root proof.\nSeven pinned files include this plan/C21 and the actual accepted inputs:\n\n| Incoming file | Exact raw/LF SHA256 unless noted |\n|---|---|\n|211 current handoff|0d14506e314a11fef0637cc66cf29036f174b94cafbf7fa5ede2eff88937500f|\n|212 current handoff|4da6e5b4f0a70273d78c067f34484c8a5f6faf164b0f09c1559b9a73ff6611fe|\n|212 independent review|79429b9f1750710baae46751a5792e4a02e7c177888a01f5ca3a15c4039a78f7|\n|212 current QC|73bd2a2447b38c9d95cbc3bd69b8037e0f46b7564655b4513009fd6707b7b07d|\n|212 paragraaf MD, raw|9350d60fadee3494124f7b0593bc1efcf00db5ea292d0a19fc3f10518e11d1f8|\n\nNo assumed mastery follows from these records. Book1 familiarity is not a\nsubstitute for the printed formal instruction. Later232 must separately teach\ninverse supply as successive-unit marginal cost; this paragraph's batch-average\ndefinition does not silently authorize that new interpretation. No protected\nunit metadata or formal output-choice extension is commissioned here.\n\n## 6. Core visuals and accessibility\n\n| SVG/PNG pair in_assets | Role and location |\n|---|---|\n|2.1.3_fig_1|Same-day holders0/10/20 and TK20/50/100 with matched interval arrows; theory|\n|2.1.3_fig_2|Ratios30/10=3 and50/10=5 at correct right endpoints; theory|\n|2.1.3_fig_3|Corresponding TO0/80/160, MO8 and fixed-price condition; theory|\n|2.1.3_fig_4|Separated total-profit versus per-extra-product growth cards; theory|\n|2.1.3_we_1|Complete Lus/Bout interval comparison with supplied totals and ratios; worked example|\n|2.1.3_ex_1|Patches first interval worked, second blank with endpoint convention; optional guided work|\n\nThese are table/procedure diagrams, not economic coordinate graphs. Keep dark\narrows, printed units, labels and grouping; no relationsh